  "limits": [
    "Timings are individual observations under concurrent verification, not a general performance guarantee. The first-owner scale probe combines 4/8/16/32/64 initially null bindings, delayed setters and one reader; the loop scale probe retains its baseline sources.",
    "The 10000-iteration native stress asserts one live deferred record at peak. The complete fixture peaks at four records/120bytes. One injected registration failure publishes no binding; records, callable images and regions are released exactly once.",
    "Positive cases cover ordinary zero/one/repeated loops, per-iteration and accumulated actions, lexical/regional/field/callable targets, declared borrowed helper results, delayed effects, chained assignments, shadowing, checked-null recovery, writes after binding and retained borrows through a local transfer or failure before it.",
    "Invalid cases reject incompatible owners, expired or uninitialized storage, const/readonly violations, failed registration and consumed owning names. A supplemental conditional-consumption case also rejects.",
    "The valid branch-region probe acquires its region and registers cleanup on the same branch. Its joined owner and queue facts still lose that correlation and reject; this is an implementation gap rather than a language restriction.",
    "Non-queryable owner provenance, remaining loop/target/result correlations, ownership mutation and owning operands during cleanup, generic capture transport, process-lifetime module queues and broader callable-family/AOT work remain unfinished.",
    "Inferred owners remain one statically consistent owner. Existing owning slots supply its base across local transfers; this selects a handle retaining the same region, not a runtime actual-owner union. No region layout, allocator, ABI, runtime ownership table, D-16 fraction behavior or D-22 construction choice is changed."
  ]
